At face value, 32.1\% temporal C\% suggests substantial item-level instability. The near-zero sanity check (0.21\%) confirms the signal is non-trivial. However, several warning signs emerge: (a)~within-family DIF tracks architecture changes (Llama-2$\to$3: 58.7\%, reflecting GQA and RoPE scaling changes) rather than training data shifts; (b)~enrichment against web-overlap labels is $\approx$1.0, indicating DIF flags are orthogonal to known contamination proxies; (c)~domain-level correlation is weak ($\rho{=}0.29$), showing no clustering in ``known contaminated'' subjects.

%% 4.2 Architecture Stratification
\subsection{Architecture Stratification Reveals the Confound}
\label{sec:exp-arch}

\begin{table}[h]
\centering
\caption{DIF statistics by architecture subgroup. Restricting to homogeneous populations dramatically reduces C\%, indicating architecture heterogeneity is the primary driver.}
\label{tab:arch-strat}
