Even within the decoder-only subgroup, IRT fit remains poor. RMSEA$=$0.063 exceeds the 0.05 threshold for acceptable fit; CFI$=$0.84 falls below the 0.90 threshold. This indicates that unidimensional IRT is misspecified for LLM populations regardless of architecture mixing.

\textbf{Non-uniform DIF.} SIBTEST analysis within the decoder-only subgroup finds 14.2\% non-uniform DIF, with only 28\% overlap against MH flags. MH misses the majority of non-uniform effects, further undermining it as the primary detection method.

%% 4.3 Item-Focused Trees
\subsection{Item-Focused Trees: Architecture Dominates Time}
\label{sec:exp-ift}

\begin{table}[h]
\centering
\caption{Variable importance from Item-Focused Trees. Architecture type is the primary split for the vast majority of items.}
\label{tab:ift}
\begin{tabular}{lccc}
